+- **step**: Initialize pose parameters $\theta$. Optimize over $L_N$ using SGD with cyclic learning rate between $1e-6$ and $1e-4$ every 100 steps and momentum 0.9 [S2]. Monitor convergence by calculating the standard deviation of $L_N$ over the last 10 iterations ($std_{L_N}$) [S2]. If $std_{L_N} < 3 \times 10^{-3}$, switch optimization to Grad-NCC similarity [S2]. Optimize over $L_{GNNC}$ using SGD with cyclic learning rate between $1e-3$ and $3e-3$ and momentum 0.9 [S2]. Stop when $std_{L_{GNNC}} < 1 \times 10^{-5}$ [S2].
 
-#### Progressive Camera Pose Generation
-- **Definition:** A training strategy that gradually increases the angular distance of sampled target viewpoints from source views to stabilize optimization [S3, unofficial].
-- **Steps:** Sample noise uniformly from interval $[-\beta, +\beta]$ and add it to original Euler rotation angles of input view poses [S3, unofficial].
-- **Parameters:** Parameter $\beta$: Grows linearly from 3 to 9 degrees throughout the course of optimization [S3, unofficial].
